[{"page":1,"text":"MINUTES OF A REDEVELOPMENT\n\nAGENCY BOARD MEETING\n\nJuly 14, 2026, at 6:58 PM\n\nPresent\n\nChair Zack Stratton\n\nBoardmember Parker McCumber\n\nBoardmember Jacob Wood\n\nBoardmember Jacob Holdaway\n\nBoardmember David Lauret\n\nBoardmember Ezra Nair\n\nAbsent\n\nStaff Present: Chief Deputy Holden Rockwell with the Utah County Sherrif’s Office, RDA\nDirector Josh Daniels, City Manager Brian Voeks, City Attorney Jesse Riddle and Deputy City\n\nRecorder Tony Lara\n\n1.\n\nCALL TO ORDER\n\nChair Stratton called the meeting to order at 6:58pm\n\n2.\n\nWORK SESSION\n\n2.1. RDA Advisors Update\n\nKim Cornelius provided a brief update on the advisors’ work, noting that they were approximately\nthree weeks into their review and continued to familiarize themselves with RDA matters. He stated that\nmonthly invoices would include a synopsis of work completed during the billing period and that a more\ncomprehensive report would be provided at a later date.\n\nJared Tamez provided an update regarding concerns with midge flies near Utah Lake, noting\nthat he had contacted the Utah Lake Authority to explore the issue. He reported that graduate\ninterns may study the matter during an upcoming semester to gather data and identify potential\napproaches that balance impacts on residents with the environmental benefits of the species.\n\n3.\n\nPUBLIC COMMENTS\n\nDaria Evans, living in the Villas neighborhood, asked for clarification regarding the parcels\nincluded in the proposed RDA triggering action, including the extent of the area identified as\nJames Bay, whether the Orchards was also being triggered, and why property records listed the\nCity under both “Vineyard City” and “Town of Vineyard.” She also questioned why her\ncommunity’s clubhouse was included as a separate parcel and sought clarification regarding the\ninclusion of tax-exempt and common-area properties in the triggering action.\nChip Price, living in the Providence neighborhood, asked for clarification regarding the\nPage 1 of 3; July 14, 2026, Redevelopment Agency Board Agenda","ocr":false},{"page":2,"text":"purpose and operation of the RDA, specifically whether it was established to facilitate cleanup and\nredevelopment of the former Geneva Steel property. He asked whether developers are able to\nutilize RDA funding to offset environmental cleanup costs associated with preparing contaminated\nproperty for development.\n\n4.\n\nCONSENT ITEMS\n\n4.1. Approval of June 23, 2026, RDA Meeting Minutes\n\n4.2. Approval of the July 7, 2026, RDA Meeting Minutes\n\nMotion: BOARDMEMBER LAURET MOVED TO APPROVE THE CONSENT ITEMS\n\nAS PRESENTED. BOARDMEMBER MCCUMBER SECONDED. BOARDMEMBERS NAIR,\n\nLAURET, WOOD, HOLDAWAY AND MCCUMBER VOTED YES. THE MOTION PASSED\n\nUNANIMOUSLY.\n\n5.\n\nBUSINESS ITEMS\n\n5.1. Approve Resolution U2026-04 Authorizing the RDA Director to Trigger Tax\n\nIncrement Financing Collection for Designated Parcels\n\nThe Board discussed the proposed triggering of additional parcels within the RDA project area,\nincluding the anticipated tax increment, allocation of remaining base value, and effects on future\nCity tax revenues. RDA Director Josh Daniels explained the methodology used to identify and\nvalue parcels within the James Bay and Orchards areas, including developed, tax-exempt, and\ncommon-area properties. During public comment, Daria Evans asked questions regarding the\nparcels included in the proposed triggering, property ownership designations, and the inclusion of\ncommunity common areas; staff clarified the parcel data and rationale for triggering developed\nareas at this stage of the RDA.\n\nMotion: BOARDMEMBER HOLDAWAY MOVED TO TABLE THE ITEM.\n\nTHERE WAS NO SECOND. THE MOTION FAILED.\nMotion: BOARDMEMBER LAURET MOVED TO ADOPT RESOLUTION U202604 AUTHORIZING THE RDA DIRECTOR TO TRIGGER TAX INCREMEMNT\n\nFINANCING COLLECTION FOR DESIGNATED PARCELS. BOARDMEMBER\n\nMCCUMBER SECONDED. THE ROLL CALL WAS AS FOLLOWS: CHAIR\n\nSTRATTON AND BOARDMEMBERS NAIR, LAURET, WOOD, AND MCCUMBER\n\nVOTED YES. BOARDMEMBER HOLDAWAY VOTED NO. THE MOTION PASSED.\n\n6.\n\nADJOURNMENT\n\nThe meeting was adjourned at 7:30\n\nMINUTES APPROVED ON: August 25, 2026\nPage 2 of 3; July 14, 2026, Redevelopment Agency Board Agenda","ocr":false},{"page":3,"text":"CERTIFIED CORRECT BY:\n\nTONY LARA, DEPUTY CITY RECORDER\n\nPage 3 of 3; July 14, 2026, Redevelopment Agency Board Agenda","ocr":false}]